{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDbqrdgKA3HqXrHfhLmJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RxQfbGfukoZzsHY3JFUga7","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-batch-6bpo831o/agent && S=../skill/scripts; P=/Users/brenn/.cache/uv/builds-v0/.tmpR1cD4H/bin/python; F=brace-findings.json\na(){ $P $S/answer.py $F \"$@\" || echo \"FAILED: $*\"; }\n# R09\na check R09.1 --met no --evidence config/budgets.yaml:2 --quote \"run:\" --note \"Only static per-run caps exist. No rule evaluates a sequence of calls (many reads then an outside send). Searched src, config, k8s, infra for sequence/detect/anomaly rules: none.\"\na check R09.2 --met no --evidence config/budgets.yaml:8 --quote \"maxToolCalls: 16\" --note \"Static hard caps on tool calls, not detection of unusual fan-out. The intent classifier call at src/agent/classifier.ts:45 is outside the budget meter. No alerting on unusual usage.\"\na check R09.3 --met no --evidence config/budgets.yaml:5 --quote \"maxInputTokens: 120000      # summed across model calls in the run\" --note \"One fleet-wide value for every context size. No per-context-size-range baselines or thresholds.\"\na check R09.4 --met no --evidence src/tools/executor.ts:86 --quote \"const raw = await tool.invoke(args, { clinicId, signal: d.budget.signal, runCtx: ctx, context: d.contextSize });\" --note \"Allowed tools (refund, SMS to patient on record, EHR writes) can cause harm if hijacked. High-impact calls get a staff approval only. No task-alignment checker compares the action with the original task before it runs.\"\na item R09 --rating gap --confidence high --summary \"No sequence, fan-out, per-context-size, or task-alignment detection exists; only static per-run caps.\" --next \"Add run-level sequence and fan-out rules, per-context-size-range baselines, and a task-alignment checker that never sees untrusted content before high-impact actions.\" --violates \"Test suspicious chains of actions that are each allowed on their own\"\n# R10\na item R10 --rating needs_evidence --confidence medium --summary \"No second-model or pattern review of misaligned behavior was found in the repo, and no record says misalignment is out of scope.\" --next \"Record whether deliberate misalignment is in scope. If it is, add and document an evasion review and red-team runs; if not, draft an N/A with approval.\"\n# R11\na check R11.1 --met no --evidence src/tools/executor.ts:59 --quote \"await killSwitch.assertRunning(ctx.tenantId);\" --note \"Checked before each model turn (loop.ts:57) and tool call, and a read failure fails closed. But the tool check uses ctx.tenantId while the tool acts on input.clinicId (executor.ts:63), so a halt on the target clinic's tenant#<id> does not stop a sibling-clinic call. refresh() also ignores UnprocessedKeys from BatchGet (kill-switch.ts:35).\"\na check R11.2 --met no --evidence infra/terraform/iam.tf:47 --quote 'Resource = \"arn:aws:dynamodb:${var.region}:${data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id}:table/clinic-agent-*\"' --note \"The agent runtime role has dynamodb:PutItem and UpdateItem on table/clinic-agent-*, which matches clinic-agent-control. The agent's own credentials can set, clear, or overwrite the stop flag. kill-switch.ts:6 says the agent only reads it.\"\na check R11.3 --met no --evidence src/integrations/eligibility-a2a.ts:36 --quote \"const res = await fetch(env.tokenExchangeUrl, {\" --note \"This fetch in the eligibility tool has no signal or timeout, so a running call is not cancelled at stop. The reminders worker registers with killSwitch but never starts the watcher (reminders.ts:27), so its in-flight calls are not aborted.\"\na check R11.4 --met no --evidence src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts:65 --quote \"sessions.set(clinicId, client);\" --note \"EHR MCP sessions are closed only by a 4-minute timer. The stop path (kill-switch.ts) aborts signals and closes no session or stream.\"\na check R11.5 --met no --evidence infra/terraform/iam.tf:47 --quote 'Resource = \"arn:aws:dynamodb:${var.region}:${data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id}:table/clinic-agent-*\"' --note \"The ops role is limited to the on-call SSO group (iam.tf:66), but the agent runtime role can also write the control table, so not only named operators can set the stop.\"\na flag R11 --evidence infra/terraform/iam.tf:47 --note \"Runtime role can write clinic-agent-control, so the agent's credentials can change the stop flag\"\na flag R11 --evidence src/workers/reminders.ts:27 --note \"Reminders worker never starts the kill-switch watcher; in-flight work is not aborted. No dated drill or maximum stop time found in the repo.\"\na item R11 --rating gap --confidence high --summary \"The agent's runtime role can write the stop flag, and running calls and open sessions are not reliably cancelled.\" --next \"Scope the runtime role to exclude clinic-agent-control, add signals and timeouts to all outbound calls, close sessions on stop, start the watcher in the worker, and run a dated drill.\" --violates \"The agent's credentials must not be able to change it.\"\n# R12\na check R12.1 --met no --evidence config/policy.yaml:5 --quote \"highImpactTools:\" --note \"Policy lists only approval-gated tools. No per-operation stop behavior (cancel, complete, reconcile) is stated for refunds, SMS, or EHR writes.\"\na check R12.2 --met unknown --note \"No queue or retry code exists beyond the SDK's one model retry (loop.ts:15) and CronJob backoffLimit 0. The inbound SMS reply at sms-webhook.ts:73 is still sent after a stop. Could not tell from the repo whether this counts as a queued action.\"\na check R12.3 --met no --evidence src/workflows/eligibility-check.ts:40 --quote \"const refund = await payments.refundDeposit(\" --note \"A refund aborted mid-flight has an unknown outcome. The only handling is tool.failed or run.stopped (executor.ts:93, loop.ts:107). No tracked hold, owner, or block on dependent actions.\"\na check R12.4 --met unknown --note \"No checkpoint or auto-resume exists. Reminders CronJob has restartPolicy Never and backoffLimit 0 (deployment.yaml:133), but the next scheduled run starts unattended and only the persistent flag stops it. Cluster-level restart behavior is outside this repo.\"\na check R12.5 --met unknown --note \"Stop revokes no credentials. Runs are gated by the flag and credentials are short-lived (IRSA 3600s, EHR token 5 min), but the stop path has no revocation. Not enough to rate from the repo.\"\na flag R12 --evidence src/workflows/eligibility-check.ts:40 --note \"Deposit refund inside the eligibility tool has no stop policy or reconcile hold\"\na item R12 --rating gap --confidence medium --summary \"No per-operation stop policy or tracked hold exists for in-flight or unclear outside actions.\" --next \"Define cancel/complete/reconcile per operation and add a tracked hold with an owner for aborted refunds and SMS sends.\" --violates \"Decide what happens to writes in progress, queued actions, and outside side effects.\"\n# R13\na check R13.1 --met no --evidence src/tools/executor.ts:89 --quote 'await audit.record({ ...base, event: \"tool.executed\", approvalId, detail: { clinicId } });' --note \"The tool.executed record has no key arguments and no result. model.decision lists only proposed tool id and name (loop.ts:73). The audit write comes after the tool has already run.\"\na check R13.2 --met no --evidence src/tools/executor.ts:47 --quote \"policyVersion: policy.version,\" --note \"config/policy.yaml:2 defines policyVersion, but the Policy type and this line read policy.version, which is undefined at runtime, so the policy version is never recorded. Budget and halt denials throw and are logged only as run.stopped with no tool or policy version.\"\na check R13.3 --met unknown --note \"tool.executed passes approvalId (executor.ts:89), but a full coverage ledger was not built. The eligibility tool's refund (eligibility-check.ts:45) has no approvalId.\"\na check R13.4 --met no --evidence src/agent/loop.ts:61 --quote \"const res = await anthropic.messages.create({ ...req, max_tokens: 1024 }, { signal: budget.signal });\" --note \"A failed or retried model call (maxRetries 1 at loop.ts:15) writes no step. Halted, budget, and abort errors from a tool rethrow (executor.ts:92) and become a run.stopped record with no tool or toolUseId (loop.ts:107).\"\na check R13.5 --met unknown --note \"Harness code writes the records and the model has no audit tool. Not rated yes because no coverage ledger was built. The tool record is written only after the tool runs (executor.ts:89).\"\na flag R13 --evidence config/policy.yaml:2 --note \"policyVersion key in YAML is read as policy.version, so audit records omit the policy version\"\na item R13 --rating gap --confidence high --summary \"Audit records omit the policy version, tool arguments and results, and failed model or aborted-tool steps.\" --next \"Read policyVersion correctly, record key arguments and results, and write linked steps for model errors, retries, and aborted tool calls.\" --violates \"authorization decisions with the policy version used\"\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7619,"cache_read_input_tokens":68279,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7619},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"103fe82b-a374-427e-baf1-db53e5caca42","uuid":"9ff52ff5-14d4-4ec9-8437-96585997a383","timestamp":"2026-10-20T13:54:22.721Z","request_id":"req_011CgDbqrL4wc9So7nQrcWYg","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01RxQfbGfukoZzsHY3JFUga7":{"command":"cd /private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-batch-6bpo831o/agent && S=../skill/scripts; P=/Users/brenn/.cache/uv/builds-v0/.tmpR1cD4H/bin/python; F=brace-findings.json\na(){ $P $S/answer.py $F \"$@\" || echo \"FAILED: $*\"; }\n# R09\na check R09.1 --met no --evidence config/budgets.yaml:2 --quote \"run:\" --note \"Only static per-run caps exist. No rule evaluates a sequence of calls (many reads then an outside send). Searched src, config, k8s, infra for sequence/detect/anomaly rules: none.\"\na check R09.2 --met no --evidence config/budgets.yaml:8 --quote \"maxToolCalls: 16\" --note \"Static hard caps on tool calls, not detection of unusual fan-out. The intent classifier call at src/agent/classifier.ts:45 is outside the budget meter. No alerting on unusual usage.\"\na check R09.3 --met no --evidence config/budgets.yaml:5 --quote \"maxInputTokens: 120000      # summed across model calls in the run\" --note \"One fleet-wide value for every context size. No per-context-size-range baselines or thresholds.\"\na check R09.4 --met no --evidence src/tools/executor.ts:86 --quote \"const raw = await tool.invoke(args, { clinicId, signal: d.budget.signal, runCtx: ctx, context: d.contextSize });\" --note \"Allowed tools (refund, SMS to patient on record, EHR writes) can cause harm if hijacked. High-impact calls get a staff approval only. No task-alignment checker compares the action with the original task before it runs.\"\na item R09 --rating gap --confidence high --summary \"No sequence, fan-out, per-context-size, or task-alignment detection exists; only static per-run caps.\" --next \"Add run-level sequence and fan-out rules, per-context-size-range baselines, and a task-alignment checker that never sees untrusted content before high-impact actions.\" --violates \"Test suspicious chains of actions that are each allowed on their own\"\n# R10\na item R10 --rating needs_evidence --confidence medium --summary \"No second-model or pattern review of misaligned behavior was found in the repo, and no record says misalignment is out of scope.\" --next \"Record whether deliberate misalignment is in scope. If it is, add and document an evasion review and red-team runs; if not, draft an N/A with approval.\"\n# R11\na check R11.1 --met no --evidence src/tools/executor.ts:59 --quote \"await killSwitch.assertRunning(ctx.tenantId);\" --note \"Checked before each model turn (loop.ts:57) and tool call, and a read failure fails closed. But the tool check uses ctx.tenantId while the tool acts on input.clinicId (executor.ts:63), so a halt on the target clinic's tenant#<id> does not stop a sibling-clinic call. refresh() also ignores UnprocessedKeys from BatchGet (kill-switch.ts:35).\"\na check R11.2 --met no --evidence infra/terraform/iam.tf:47 --quote 'Resource = \"arn:aws:dynamodb:${var.region}:${data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id}:table/clinic-agent-*\"' --note \"The agent runtime role has dynamodb:PutItem and UpdateItem on table/clinic-agent-*, which matches clinic-agent-control. The agent's own credentials can set, clear, or overwrite the stop flag. kill-switch.ts:6 says the agent only reads it.\"\na check R11.3 --met no --evidence src/integrations/eligibility-a2a.ts:36 --quote \"const res = await fetch(env.tokenExchangeUrl, {\" --note \"This fetch in the eligibility tool has no signal or timeout, so a running call is not cancelled at stop. The reminders worker registers with killSwitch but never starts the watcher (reminders.ts:27), so its in-flight calls are not aborted.\"\na check R11.4 --met no --evidence src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts:65 --quote \"sessions.set(clinicId, client);\" --note \"EHR MCP sessions are closed only by a 4-minute timer. The stop path (kill-switch.ts) aborts signals and closes no session or stream.\"\na check R11.5 --met no --evidence infra/terraform/iam.tf:47 --quote 'Resource = \"arn:aws:dynamodb:${var.region}:${data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id}:table/clinic-agent-*\"' --note \"The ops role is limited to the on-call SSO group (iam.tf:66), but the agent runtime role can also write the control table, so not only named operators can set the stop.\"\na flag R11 --evidence infra/terraform/iam.tf:47 --note \"Runtime role can write clinic-agent-control, so the agent's credentials can change the stop flag\"\na flag R11 --evidence src/workers/reminders.ts:27 --note \"Reminders worker never starts the kill-switch watcher; in-flight work is not aborted. No dated drill or maximum stop time found in the repo.\"\na item R11 --rating gap --confidence high --summary \"The agent's runtime role can write the stop flag, and running calls and open sessions are not reliably cancelled.\" --next \"Scope the runtime role to exclude clinic-agent-control, add signals and timeouts to all outbound calls, close sessions on stop, start the watcher in the worker, and run a dated drill.\" --violates \"The agent's credentials must not be able to change it.\"\n# R12\na check R12.1 --met no --evidence config/policy.yaml:5 --quote \"highImpactTools:\" --note \"Policy lists only approval-gated tools. No per-operation stop behavior (cancel, complete, reconcile) is stated for refunds, SMS, or EHR writes.\"\na check R12.2 --met unknown --note \"No queue or retry code exists beyond the SDK's one model retry (loop.ts:15) and CronJob backoffLimit 0. The inbound SMS reply at sms-webhook.ts:73 is still sent after a stop. Could not tell from the repo whether this counts as a queued action.\"\na check R12.3 --met no --evidence src/workflows/eligibility-check.ts:40 --quote \"const refund = await payments.refundDeposit(\" --note \"A refund aborted mid-flight has an unknown outcome. The only handling is tool.failed or run.stopped (executor.ts:93, loop.ts:107). No tracked hold, owner, or block on dependent actions.\"\na check R12.4 --met unknown --note \"No checkpoint or auto-resume exists. Reminders CronJob has restartPolicy Never and backoffLimit 0 (deployment.yaml:133), but the next scheduled run starts unattended and only the persistent flag stops it. Cluster-level restart behavior is outside this repo.\"\na check R12.5 --met unknown --note \"Stop revokes no credentials. Runs are gated by the flag and credentials are short-lived (IRSA 3600s, EHR token 5 min), but the stop path has no revocation. Not enough to rate from the repo.\"\na flag R12 --evidence src/workflows/eligibility-check.ts:40 --note \"Deposit refund inside the eligibility tool has no stop policy or reconcile hold\"\na item R12 --rating gap --confidence medium --summary \"No per-operation stop policy or tracked hold exists for in-flight or unclear outside actions.\" --next \"Define cancel/complete/reconcile per operation and add a tracked hold with an owner for aborted refunds and SMS sends.\" --violates \"Decide what happens to writes in progress, queued actions, and outside side effects.\"\n# R13\na check R13.1 --met no --evidence src/tools/executor.ts:89 --quote 'await audit.record({ ...base, event: \"tool.executed\", approvalId, detail: { clinicId } });' --note \"The tool.executed record has no key arguments and no result. model.decision lists only proposed tool id and name (loop.ts:73). The audit write comes after the tool has already run.\"\na check R13.2 --met no --evidence src/tools/executor.ts:47 --quote \"policyVersion: policy.version,\" --note \"config/policy.yaml:2 defines policyVersion, but the Policy type and this line read policy.version, which is undefined at runtime, so the policy version is never recorded. Budget and halt denials throw and are logged only as run.stopped with no tool or policy version.\"\na check R13.3 --met unknown --note \"tool.executed passes approvalId (executor.ts:89), but a full coverage ledger was not built. The eligibility tool's refund (eligibility-check.ts:45) has no approvalId.\"\na check R13.4 --met no --evidence src/agent/loop.ts:61 --quote \"const res = await anthropic.messages.create({ ...req, max_tokens: 1024 }, { signal: budget.signal });\" --note \"A failed or retried model call (maxRetries 1 at loop.ts:15) writes no step. Halted, budget, and abort errors from a tool rethrow (executor.ts:92) and become a run.stopped record with no tool or toolUseId (loop.ts:107).\"\na check R13.5 --met unknown --note \"Harness code writes the records and the model has no audit tool. Not rated yes because no coverage ledger was built. The tool record is written only after the tool runs (executor.ts:89).\"\na flag R13 --evidence config/policy.yaml:2 --note \"policyVersion key in YAML is read as policy.version, so audit records omit the policy version\"\na item R13 --rating gap --confidence high --summary \"Audit records omit the policy version, tool arguments and results, and failed model or aborted-tool steps.\" --next \"Read policyVersion correctly, record key arguments and results, and write linked steps for model errors, retries, and aborted tool calls.\" --violates \"authorization decisions with the policy version used\"\n"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RxQfbGfukoZzsHY3JFUga7","type":"tool_result","content":"Saved R09.1 = no. Next: R09.2 — Rules cover unusual fan-out and resource use.\n  How to verify: 1) Read detection rules. 2) Check rules for unusual fan-out (sub-agents, parallel calls) and resource use. 3) Answer no if neither is covered.\nSaved R09.2 = no. Next: R09.3 — Thresholds or baselines are set per context-size range, not as one fleet-wide value.\n  How to verify: 1) Read rule thresholds and baselines. 2) Check they are set per context-size range. 3) Answer no if one fleet-wide value is used for all contexts.\nSaved R09.3 = no. Next: R09.4 — If hijack through allowed tools alone is possible, each high-impact action is checked against the original task before it runs, by a checker that is not given the untrusted content.\n  How to verify: 1) Check whether allowed tools alone could cause harm if the agent is hijacked. 2) If so, find a task-alignment checker before high-impact actions and see what input it receives. 3) Answer no if no checker exists, it is given the untrusted content, or its errors let the action proceed.\nSaved R09.4 = no. Next: finish item R09 with `answer.py ... item R09 --rating ...`\nSaved item R09 = gap. Next: finish item R10 with `answer.py ... item R10 --rating ...`\nSaved item R10 = needs_evidence. Next: R11.1 — A stop control halts new model calls and new tool calls when set.\n  How to verify: 1) Find the stop control (kill flag, `stop`, `halt`, feature flag, revoked token). 2) Check the loop checks it before every model call and tool call. 3) Answer no if it is checked only at run start, only between turns, a second loop or worker skips it, or a check error is treated as not stopped.\nSaved R11.1 = no. Next: R11.2 — The agent's own credentials and tools cannot set, clear, delete, or delay the stop control.\n  How to verify: 1) Find where the stop flag is stored and who can write it. 2) Compare with the agent's credentials and tools. 3) Answer no if the agent's role can write, delete, or expire the flag, a tool can reach its store, or the agent can delay it (for example by catching the stop signal).\nSaved R11.2 = no. Next: R11.3 — Tool calls already running are cancelled or bounded by a timeout when the stop is set.\n  How to verify: 1) Find the stop handler. 2) Check running tool calls are cancelled or bounded by a timeout. 3) Answer no if running calls finish with no timeout, or cancellation errors are swallowed and the call continues.\nSaved R11.3 = no. Next: R11.4 — The stop also closes open tool streams, subscriptions, and background tasks.\n  How to verify: 1) Find streams, subscriptions, and background tasks (`asyncio.create_task`, goroutines, websockets, SSE). 2) Check the stop handler closes them. 3) Answer no if any is left open, detached, or untracked.\nSaved R11.4 = no. Next: R11.5 — Only named operator identities can set the stop control.\n  How to verify: 1) Find who can set the stop (auth on the endpoint, IAM on the flag store). 2) Answer no if any authenticated user or service can set it with no named operator list. Answer unknown if access lives outside this repo.\nSaved R11.5 = no. Next: finish item R11 with `answer.py ... item R11 --rating ...`\nAdded red flag to R11.\nAdded red flag to R11.\nSaved item R11 = gap. Next: R12.1 — For each operation type, code or config states whether it can be cancelled, completed, or only reconciled after a stop.\n  How to verify: 1) Search code and config for a per-operation stop policy (cancel, complete, reconcile). 2) Answer no if any operation type the agent can run has no stated stop behavior.\nSaved R12.1 = no. Next: R12.2 — On stop, queued actions are cancelled or held, and automatic retries are turned off.\n  How to verify: 1) Find queue and retry code (`retry`, `backoff`, queue workers). 2) Check stop cancels or holds queued items and turns retries off. 3) Answer no if retries continue after stop or queued jobs still run.\nSaved R12.2 = unknown. Next: R12.3 — Unclear or in-progress outside actions go on a tracked hold with an owner, and dependent actions are blocked until reconciled.\n  How to verify: 1) Find handling of unclear or in-progress outside actions at stop. 2) Check they go on a tracked hold with an owner and block dependent actions. 3) Answer no if they are dropped, retried, or dependents proceed.\nSaved R12.3 = no. Next: R12.4 — A stopped run does not restart on its own; restart needs an operator action.\n  How to verify: 1) Find restart logic (supervisors, `restartPolicy`, cron, auto-resume). 2) Answer no if a stopped run restarts automatically (`restartPolicy: Always`, auto-resume from checkpoint) without an operator action.\nSaved R12.4 = unknown. Next: R12.5 — Workers and queued jobs lose their credentials or authority at stop, so no orphaned work can act.\n  How to verify: 1) Find workers and queued jobs and the credentials they hold. 2) Check stop revokes or expires them. 3) Answer no if workers keep long-lived credentials after stop, or jobs carry their own tokens that stay valid.\nSaved R12.5 = unknown. Next: finish item R12 with `answer.py ... item R12 --rating ...`\nAdded red flag to R12.\nSaved item R12 = gap. Next: R13.1 — Each step writes a record linked to the run: proposed action, tool call with key arguments, result, error, and timestamp.\n  How to verify: 1) Find step logging (trace spans, audit log writes). 2) Check each record has run ID, proposed action, tool call with key arguments, result, error, and timestamp. 3) Answer no if any field is missing, or logging happens only on the success branch.\nSaved R13.1 = no. Next: R13.2 — Authorization decisions are recorded with the policy version, including denials, not only allowed calls.\n  How to verify: 1) Find authorization decision code. 2) Check both allow and deny are logged with the policy version. 3) Answer no if denials are not logged, or no policy version is recorded.\nSaved R13.2 = no. Next: R13.3 — Approved actions record their approval ID.\n  How to verify: 1) Find where approved actions are logged. 2) Answer no if the approval ID is not recorded with the action.\nSaved R13.3 = unknown. Next: R13.4 — Tool errors, timeouts, and retry attempts are recorded as linked execution steps, so failed actions can be rebuilt.\n  How to verify: 1) Find error, timeout and retry branches. 2) Trace their records into the execution graph, including failed attempts and timestamps. 3) Answer no if errors or retry steps are omitted or cannot be linked to the run. Evaluate the core execution-graph requirement here; destination operation IDs are fallback/recovery evidence, not an additional core clause.\nSaved R13.4 = no. Next: R13.5 — Records are written by the harness or gateway, not by the model, and do not depend on the run's final answer.\n  How to verify: 1) Find who writes records. 2) Answer no if the model writes them via a tool, records are built from the final answer, or logging runs only if the run completes.\nSaved R13.5 = unknown. Next: finish item R13 with `answer.py ... item R13 --rating ...`\nAdded red flag to R13.\nSaved item R13 = gap. All checks and items have answers. Run validate_findings.py --fix.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"103fe82b-a374-427e-baf1-db53e5caca42","uuid":"261d20ee-0e1c-407a-ab53-f1fb929731cb","timestamp":"2026-10-20T13:54:23.559Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"Saved R09.1 = no. Next: R09.2 — Rules cover unusual fan-out and resource use.\n  How to verify: 1) Read detection rules. 2) Check rules for unusual fan-out (sub-agents, parallel calls) and resource use. 3) Answer no if neither is covered.\nSaved R09.2 = no. Next: R09.3 — Thresholds or baselines are set per context-size range, not as one fleet-wide value.\n  How to verify: 1) Read rule thresholds and baselines. 2) Check they are set per context-size range. 3) Answer no if one fleet-wide value is used for all contexts.\nSaved R09.3 = no. 