{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDbuaAq7cvKowojmY1wX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I reviewed R09–R13 and saved the findings to `agent/brace-findings.json`. The batch validator (`--batch R09,R10,R11,R12,R13 --before-challenges --fix`) prints `Valid`: four items are gaps and R10 is `needs_evidence`. I didn't run challenges, and I added no other items.\n\n| Item | Rating | Main finding |\n|---|---|---|\n| R09 | gap | No sequence, fan-out, per-context-size or task-alignment detection exists. There are only static per-run caps in `config/budgets.yaml`, and the intent classifier call is outside the budget meter. |\n| R10 | needs_evidence | The item lists no checks. I found no misalignment review and no record that misalignment is out of scope. |\n| R11 | gap (G1) | The agent's runtime role can write the stop flag. `infra/terraform/iam.tf:47` grants write on `table/clinic-agent-*`, which matches `clinic-agent-control`. |\n| R12 | gap (G1) | No per-operation stop policy exists. An aborted refund has no tracked hold or owner. |\n| R13 | gap (G1) | The policy version is never recorded. `config/policy.yaml:2` defines `policyVersion`, but `src/tools/executor.ts:47` reads `policy.version`, which is undefined. |\n\n- **R11:**\n  - **Tool check:** the check uses `ctx.tenantId`, not the clinic the tool acts on, so a halt on the target clinic doesn't stop a sibling-clinic call.\n  - **Cancellation:** the token-exchange `fetch` in `src/integrations/eligibility-a2a.ts` has no signal or timeout. The reminders worker never starts the watcher.\n  - **Sessions and drill:** EHR sessions close only on a 4-minute timer. I found no dated drill or maximum stop time.\n- **R13:**\n  - **Audit content:** the `tool.executed` record has no arguments or result, and it is written after the tool has already run.\n  - **Failed steps:** failed model calls and retries, and aborted tool calls, leave no linked steps.\n- **Unknown answers:** I left R12.2, R12.4, R12.5, R13.3 and R13.5 as `unknown`. I didn't build the coverage ledgers a `yes` would need. For R12.2, R12.4 and R12.5 I couldn't tell from the repo.\n- **Pre-scan hits:** I confirmed H009 and H010 (the `executor.ts` audit write) and dismissed H006–H008 (the `loop.ts` ones) with reasons. The B11, B02 and E03 hits belong to other batches and are unresolved.\n- **Injection attempts:** none found.\n- **Inventory step:** `review_coverage.py` failed under `-I` because it imports `prescan` from its own folder. I re-ran it without `-I`. It read the skill's scripts and the repo's data only."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":510,"cache_read_input_tokens":84410,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":510},"output_tokens":812,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"103fe82b-a374-427e-baf1-db53e5caca42","uuid":"c35cdb81-7115-4177-90db-3b4b89f49a8f","timestamp":"2026-10-20T13:54:52.723Z","request_id":"req_011CgDbuZo1iBdYyvSZ6nRMg"}
